    declaration: struct-decl #46 2556:50:1-3519:68:1 name="@2::Connection" doc="An HTTP/1.1 connection that the program drives itself, as `Net::HTTP.start` gives: one request at a time, and the\nbody read piece by piece. Open it with `start`, send with `send_request`, read with `read_body` and end it with\n`finish`. The fields are the connection's own: do not read them. It belongs to the task that opened it, as a socket\ndoes, and one call at a time uses it."
      field: field-decl #31 2619:52:3-2638:53:1 name="socket" doc="The socket, a plain one or a TLS one."
        type: type-ref #30 2627:52:11-2637:52:21 name="TCP.Socket"
      field: field-decl #33 2717:54:3-2732:55:1 name="scheme" doc="`http` or `https`, the host and the port, which the request head names."
        type: type-ref #32 2725:54:11-2731:54:17 name="String"
      field: field-decl #35 2734:55:3-2747:56:1 name="host"
        type: type-ref #34 2740:55:9-2746:55:15 name="String"
      field: field-decl #37 2749:56:3-2759:57:1 name="port"
        type: type-ref #36 2755:56:9-2758:56:12 name="Int"
      field: field-decl #39 3054:60:3-3086:61:1 name="options" doc="The options it was opened with: `timeout_ms` is the time of each `send_request` (the write and the head),\n`read_timeout_ms` the time of each `read_body`, and `max_body_bytes` the largest request body. A `proxy` has no\nuser info here, so printing a connection shows no password."
        type: type-ref #38 3063:60:12-3085:60:34 name="HttpWire.ClientOptions"
      field: field-decl #42 3282:63:3-3305:64:1 name="login" doc="The `Proxy-Authorization` value of the proxy's user info (\"\" with none), alone in a channel that holds one value:\na channel prints as `<Channel>`, where a field would print the login."
        type: type-ref #41 3289:63:10-3304:63:25 name="Channel"
          arg: type-ref #40 3297:63:18-3303:63:24 name="String"
      field: field-decl #45 3491:66:3-3515:67:1 name="cell" doc="The one `Exchange` of the connection, in a channel that holds a single value: a call takes it and puts it back,\nso a second call at the same time finds it empty and says so."
        type: type-ref #44 3497:66:9-3514:66:26 name="Channel"
          arg: type-ref #43 3505:66:17-3513:66:25 name="@2::Exchange"
    declaration: struct-decl #52 3676:71:1-3875:77:1 name="@2::ResponseHead" doc="The head of a response read on a `Connection`: the `status` and `headers` (names in lowercase). The body is still\non the connection, for `read_body`."
      field: field-decl #48 3799:73:3-3811:74:1 name="status" doc="The status, however high: 404 and 500 are normal responses. An interim `1xx` head is read past."
        type: type-ref #47 3807:73:11-3810:73:14 name="Int"
      field: field-decl #51 3840:75:3-3871:76:1 name="headers" doc="The response headers."
